{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"036ba75f278efe5d","type":"text","text":"nmap -D 10.0.0.5,10.0.0.8,ME 192.168.1.10","x":1464,"y":-519,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5e8289c9c6cdf6ec","type":"text","text":"## Scanning IDS / Firewalls","x":-409,"y":-140,"width":289,"height":60},
		{"id":"8c7c238353acbaed","type":"text","text":"IDS and Firewalls are security mechanisms intended to prevent an attacker from accessing a network.","x":0,"y":-155,"width":394,"height":90},
		{"id":"e0b66c12e8cff966","type":"text","text":"Packets Infromation","x":460,"y":-720,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3c41409d0a8eb357","type":"text","text":"Source Routing","x":460,"y":-620,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"caabad6ba0ad2d7b","type":"text","text":"Source port manipulation","x":460,"y":-520,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f262621c798af1e4","type":"text","text":"Ip Address Decoy","x":460,"y":-420,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"24d6c6c1b02e5754","type":"text","text":"Sanding bad checksum","x":460,"y":-315,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"86d6930988800dce","type":"text","text":"**IP Fragmentation Scanning** ek technique hai jisme Nmap **TCP packet ko chhote-chhote IP fragments me todkar bhejta hai**. Iska purpose kuch packet filters ya legacy firewalls ke behavior ko test karna hota hai.","x":397,"y":-920,"width":377,"height":142},
		{"id":"f3564e68c7187578","type":"text","text":"**Important:** `-f` scan type nahi hai. Ye ek **packet fragmentation option** hai jo SYN Scan (`-sS`), FIN Scan (`-sF`) aur kuch dusre scan types ke saath use hota hai.","x":885,"y":-920,"width":280,"height":142},
		{"id":"1e206e302cb0c13c","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sS -T4 -A -f -v $IP`","x":1266,"y":-878,"width":232,"height":60},
		{"id":"492c0caa4903e98e","type":"text","text":"```\n-sS : TCP SYN Scan\n-T4 : Timing\n-A  : Agresive Scan\n-f  : Fragments packets\n-v  : Verbosity\n```","x":1600,"y":-1000,"width":260,"height":182},
		{"id":"71e6980352f4db02","type":"text","text":"**paranoid** (**0**), **sneaky** (**1**), **polite** (**2**), **normal** (**3**), **aggressive** (**4**), and **insane** (**5**).","x":1541,"y":-1173,"width":368,"height":60},
		{"id":"38e6bdd39aae0805","type":"text","text":"**-A** (Aggressive scan options)\n-A = -O + -sV + -sC + --traceroute","x":1960,"y":-1073,"width":314,"height":73},
		{"id":"78552b53760e90f1","type":"text","text":"Source Routing ek IP routing technique hai jisme sender khud decide karta hai ki packet ko kaun-kaun se routers/hops se hokar destination tak jana hai.","x":892,"y":-735,"width":273,"height":145},
		{"id":"fc426ecd288d0b1d","type":"text","text":"Mera packet is route se jana chahiye:\n\nRouter A\n   ↓\nRouter C\n   ↓\nRouter D\n   ↓\nServer","x":1266,"y":-783,"width":309,"height":242},
		{"id":"e6292596b1eaea1e","type":"text","text":"+----------------------+\n| IP Header            |\n| Source Address       |\n| Destination Address  |\n| Source Route Option  |\n+----------------------+\n| Data                 |\n+----------------------+","x":1640,"y":-783,"width":212,"height":242},
		{"id":"a92332e460588d38","type":"text","text":"Router packet receive karta hai:\n\n1. IP header check karta hai.\n2. Source route option dekhta hai.\n3. Diye gaye next hop par packet forward karta hai.","x":1914,"y":-783,"width":306,"height":242},
		{"id":"d1424f41bd09c209","type":"text","text":"Types of source routing","x":2335,"y":-693,"width":208,"height":60},
		{"id":"692ed14910e46f57","type":"text","text":"Loose Source Routing (LSRR)","x":2800,"y":-509,"width":262,"height":60},
		{"id":"89cdfaf2d5b1d655","type":"text","text":"Strict Source Routing (SSRR)","x":2812,"y":-843,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c9efb2bac11a8c35","type":"text","text":"Sender exact route specify karta hai.\nHost\n |\nRouter A\n |\nRouter B\n |\nDestination","x":2785,"y":-1200,"width":305,"height":226},
		{"id":"63b4b6736e8f6980","type":"text","text":"Sender kuch routers specify karta hai, beech me aur routers add ho sakte hain.\n\nHost\n |\nRouter A\n |\n(any router)\n |\nRouter B\n |\nDestination","x":3160,"y":-639,"width":332,"height":321},
		{"id":"7d70602c682cd186","type":"text","text":"`nmap --ip-options <options> target`","x":3760,"y":-501,"width":309,"height":52},
		{"id":"4b9416c0439e48f4","type":"text","text":"`nmap --ip-options \"L 10.0.0.1 10.0.0.2\" 192.168.1.10`","x":4202,"y":-505,"width":458,"height":60},
		{"id":"1dbc4535622a1d12","type":"text","text":"`L` = Loose Source Routing","x":4306,"y":-621,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1ef1307caf4b26f1","type":"text","text":"# Source Routing Detection\n\nNetwork devices aksar:\n\n- IP source route packets drop karte hain.\n- Router configuration me disable kar dete hain.\n\nCisco devices me generally:\n\n```\nno ip source-route\n```\n\nuse kiya jata hai.","x":4760,"y":-638,"width":409,"height":326},
		{"id":"94a080e2da57f387","type":"text","text":"Source Routing is an IP routing mechanism where the sender specifies the path that a packet should follow through the network. It uses IP header options such as Strict Source Routing and Loose Source Routing. Due to security risks, modern networks usually disable source routing.","x":5300,"y":-558,"width":400,"height":166},
		{"id":"cf31724c2d862732","type":"text","text":"**Strict Source Routing (SSRR)** source routing ka ek type hai jisme **sender packet ke liye exact route (exact routers/hops) specify karta hai**. Packet ko **sirf wahi path follow karna hota hai jo sender ne diya hai**.\n\nSimple words:\n\n> Sender bolta hai: \"Packet ko inhi routers se hokar jana hai, koi dusra route nahi lena.\"","x":3160,"y":-953,"width":420,"height":280},
		{"id":"cd6494b29fea2a74","type":"text","text":"Sender packet me route add karta hai:\n\n```\nSource\n |\nRouter A\n |\nRouter B\n |\nDestination\n```\n\nPacket ke IP header me:","x":3740,"y":-970,"width":329,"height":314},
		{"id":"8a4e0763ea46fd25","type":"text","text":"Host A\n  |\n  |  Packet + SSRR option\n  |\n  v\nRouter 1\n  |\n  v\nRouter 2\n  |\n  v\nServer","x":4180,"y":-966,"width":203,"height":307},
		{"id":"e5d8ee95b506fd4d","type":"text","text":"Agar Router 1 ke baad Router 3 aana chahiye tha, to packet reject/drop ho sakta hai kyunki route match nahi karta.","x":4502,"y":-874,"width":258,"height":122},
		{"id":"77feb199b364ac82","type":"text","text":"| Strict Source Routing       | Loose Source Routing                 |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Exact route define hota hai | Kuch routers define hote hain        |\n| Har hop mandatory hota hai  | Beech me extra routers aa sakte hain |\n| Zyada restrictive           | Flexible                             |\n| SSRR                        | LSRR                                 |\n","x":4367,"y":-1160,"width":529,"height":169},
		{"id":"38d57f2b49aba1bb","type":"text","text":"Loose","x":5107,"y":-972,"width":76,"height":60},
		{"id":"91ef02abab0c1736","type":"text","text":"Strict","x":5107,"y":-1260,"width":70,"height":60},
		{"id":"7ae74db7cbf191b9","type":"text","text":"A → B → C → D","x":5278,"y":-1260,"width":147,"height":60},
		{"id":"5f754560ccd2a62c","type":"text","text":"A → B → (Any Router) → D","x":5278,"y":-972,"width":230,"height":60},
		{"id":"955bae31de1ee487","type":"text","text":"Security Issues\n\nSSRR ka misuse ho sakta hai:\n\nTraffic ko unwanted path par bhejna.\nNetwork monitoring bypass karne ki koshish.\nInternal network structure reveal karna.\n\nIsliye modern networks me:\n\nRouters aksar SSRR disable kar dete hain.\nFirewalls source-routed packets drop kar dete hain.","x":5760,"y":-1260,"width":416,"height":290},
		{"id":"85f24346c7cffc24","type":"text","text":"Nmap IP options ke through source routing support karta hai:\n\n```\nnmap --ip-options \"S <router1> <router2>\" target\n```\n\n`S` = Strict Source Routing","x":6300,"y":-1197,"width":487,"height":165},
		{"id":"3de366aae1b920d9","type":"text","text":"Strict Source Routing is an IP source routing method where the sender specifies the complete and exact path that an IP packet must follow. Every router in the specified path is mandatory, and if the route cannot be followed, the packet is discarded. Due to security risks, modern networks usually disable SSRR.","x":6920,"y":-1197,"width":440,"height":165},
		{"id":"635970071d9a7033","type":"text","text":"source port 1 technique hai jisame IDS/FIREWALL ko bypass karane ke liye port number ko manually change kiya jata hai common port ke sath","x":892,"y":-540,"width":307,"height":100},
		{"id":"1ea7dd128e6d55b1","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/port_manupulation.png","x":1266,"y":-520,"width":399,"height":120},
		{"id":"e456385c3accd132","type":"text","text":"`-g` ya `--source-port` option hi help se ham ye port manupulation perform kar sakate h","x":1758,"y":-520,"width":191,"height":120},
		{"id":"6efa8a9a1c6aa3e3","type":"text","text":"`nmap -g 80 $IP`","x":2062,"y":-492,"width":158,"height":60},
		{"id":"a6d733485d0d61f9","type":"text","text":"Ip decoy 1 technique hai firwall or IDS ko bypass karane ki jisame `scanner apne real IP address ke saath kuch fake (decoy) IP addresses bhi include karta hai, taaki target ko lage ki scan multiple different machines se aa raha hai.`","x":950,"y":-390,"width":499,"height":115},
		{"id":"58a5bcbcdc4230a6","type":"text","text":"`nmap -D <decoy1,decoy2,...,ME> <target>`","x":1559,"y":-362,"width":355,"height":60},
		{"id":"f9617306500bfe5a","type":"text","text":"`nmap -D 10.0.0.5,10.0.0.8,ME 192.168.1.10`","x":1559,"y":-277,"width":359,"height":60},
		{"id":"3131887a33f25565","type":"text","text":"`nmap -D RND:5 192.168.1.10`","x":1559,"y":-200,"width":359,"height":60},
		{"id":"804e3668898daf1f","type":"text","text":"### 2. Logs aur IDS detect kar sakte hain\n\nModern security systems:\n\n- Packet patterns\n- Timing\n- TCP fingerprints\n\ndekhkar identify kar sakte hain ki scan ek hi source se aa raha hai.","x":2035,"y":-377,"width":404,"height":260},
		{"id":"29df39d303018cbb","type":"text","text":"IP Address Decoy is an Nmap technique where additional fake source IP addresses are used along with the real scanner IP during scanning. The target sees scan traffic coming from multiple sources, making the original scanner harder to identify. It is performed using the Nmap `-D` option.","x":2543,"y":-372,"width":306,"height":250},
		{"id":"1c25730a2d7cddfb","type":"text","text":"Sending Bad Checksum ek packet manipulation technique hai jisme intentionally galat (invalid) checksum wala network packet bheja jata hai taaki target system ke response behavior ko observe kiya ja sake.","x":460,"y":-185,"width":370,"height":150},
		{"id":"0c6696d4aae1cc85","type":"text","text":"Checksum ka kaam hota hai:\n\n- Packet data ki integrity check karna.\n- Detect karna ki packet corrupt hua hai ya nahi.","x":892,"y":-170,"width":421,"height":120},
		{"id":"de0cf85e21f11a6f","type":"text","text":"### Checksum kya hota hai?\n\nTCP/UDP/IP header me ek field hota hai:\n+----------------------+\n| Source Port           |\n| Destination Port      |\n| Sequence Number       |\n| Checksum  <-----------|\n+----------------------+","x":967,"y":-16,"width":346,"height":276},
		{"id":"d94daa271d7c6ba2","type":"text","text":"Checksum ek calculated value hoti hai jo packet ke data se banti hai.\n\nReceiver:\n\n1. Packet receive karta hai.\n2. Dobara checksum calculate karta hai.\n3. Compare karta hai.\n\nAgar match:\n\n```\nPacket Valid\n```\n\nAgar match nahi:\n\n```\nPacket Invalid\n```","x":1380,"y":-16,"width":379,"height":456},
		{"id":"6d36c81e99b0a640","type":"text","text":"Why send Bad Checksum?\n\nSecurity testing me:\n\nNetwork device ka behavior test karne ke liye.\nIDS/IPS aur firewall packet validation check karne ke liye.\nStack fingerprinting/research ke liye.","x":1840,"y":-16,"width":458,"height":185},
		{"id":"da06424e048d34b1","type":"text","text":"Sending Bad Checksum is a packet manipulation technique where a packet with an invalid checksum is intentionally sent to a target. The receiver should discard such packets because the checksum verification fails. It is used for network stack testing, IDS/firewall analysis, and research on packet handling behavior.","x":1840,"y":300,"width":540,"height":160},
		{"id":"f88e074faec6eb8a","type":"text","text":"`nmap --badsum 192.168.1.10`","x":1840,"y":200,"width":458,"height":60},
		{"id":"d1e4eb9414323c30","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/ip_spoofing.png","x":940,"y":502,"width":400,"height":138},
		{"id":"1552cf59d3baba2e","type":"text","text":"Blind Ip Spoofing","x":1468,"y":502,"width":178,"height":27},
		{"id":"bc19fe449ef1099d","type":"text","text":"Reflection Attack","x":1468,"y":613,"width":172,"height":27},
		{"id":"ef9ec1d40f38bc8b","type":"text","text":"Non-Blind Spoofing","x":1468,"y":558,"width":178,"height":27},
		{"id":"41983f4558996483","type":"text","text":"Attacker target ka response directly nahi dekh sakta.","x":1759,"y":502,"width":424,"height":27},
		{"id":"176cfbf0209083aa","type":"text","text":"Attacker same network me hota hai aur responses observe kar sakta hai.","x":1759,"y":558,"width":575,"height":27},
		{"id":"247ace6d9cea811f","type":"text","text":"Attacker fake source IP use karke requests dusre servers ko bhejta hai.","x":1759,"y":613,"width":562,"height":27},
		{"id":"60fa46fd153e8b78","type":"text","text":"IP Spoofing ka use kahan hota hai?\n- Legitimate Uses\n- Network testing\n- Security research\n- Firewall testing\n- Privacy research\n##### Malicious Uses\n- DDoS attacks\n- Identity hiding\n- Fake traffic generation\n- Reflection attacks","x":2520,"y":286,"width":292,"height":354},
		{"id":"5f743c08be380c7a","type":"text","text":"| IP Spoofing                         | IP Decoy                           |\n| ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| Packet ka source IP fake karta hai  | Multiple fake sources dikhata hai  |\n| General packet technique hai        | Mostly scanning technique          |\n| Responses fake IP par ja sakte hain | Scanner multiple IPs use karta hai |\n","x":2900,"y":396,"width":558,"height":134},
		{"id":"5bcd153765a865ff","type":"text","text":"IP Spoofing is a technique where the source IP address in an IP packet is modified to make it appear as if the packet came from a different host. It is used in security testing but can also be abused in attacks such as DDoS and reflection attacks.","x":3520,"y":396,"width":493,"height":134},
		{"id":"ad0d55837545a240","type":"text","text":"**MAC Address Spoofing ek technique hai jisme network device ke original MAC address ko change karke kisi dusre MAC address jaisa dikhaya jata hai.**","x":825,"y":680,"width":524,"height":89},
		{"id":"688a6063c7b8800e","type":"text","text":"MAC Filtering Bypass\nAgar router allow karta hai:\n\n```\nAllowed MAC:\nAA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF\n```\n\nAttacker MAC change karke same bana sakta hai.\n\nMAC Impersonation -> Ek device dusre device ki identity copy kar sakta hai.\nNetwork Attacks \nMAC spoofing ka use kuch Layer 2 attacks me ho sakta hai, jaise:\n\n- ARP spoofing\n- MAC flooding","x":1442,"y":660,"width":598,"height":375},
		{"id":"b71c656335e03d44","type":"text","text":"| MAC Spoofing                 | IP Spoofing                     |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| Layer 2 par kaam karta hai   | Layer 3 par kaam karta hai      |\n| MAC address change karta hai | IP address change karta hai     |\n| Local network me effective   | Internet level par bhi possible |\n| Switches ke saath related    | Routers ke saath related        |\n","x":2171,"y":660,"width":495,"height":169},
		{"id":"c15f3e063c885a65","type":"text","text":"MAC Address Spoofing is the process of changing the MAC address of a network interface to impersonate another device or hide the original hardware identity. It operates at the Data Link Layer and is used for privacy, testing, or can be abused to bypass MAC-based access controls.","x":2171,"y":860,"width":495,"height":140},
		{"id":"17e0749491c88c0e","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sT -Pn --spoof-mac 0 [Target IP]`","x":825,"y":788,"width":524,"height":60},
		{"id":"9023a80b2f852a20","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sT -Pn --spoof-mac [vendor] [Target IP]`","x":825,"y":860,"width":524,"height":60},
		{"id":"54139f4dc46c153f","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sT -Pn --spoof-mac [new mac] [Target IP]`","x":825,"y":940,"width":524,"height":60},
		{"id":"0c54d3b72c6b3fc6","type":"text","text":"Anonymizer","x":395,"y":1005,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"713defd149c683d7","type":"text","text":"Creating Custom packets","x":395,"y":1105,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"54aad6107ba41d69","type":"text","text":"Randomizing Host order","x":395,"y":1205,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"6feeed79b9a0f2fa","type":"text","text":"Proxy server","x":395,"y":1302,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c9b1895a02494c73","type":"text","text":"Firewall/IDS ko bypass karane ke liye ip spoofing ki help li jati hai. ip spoofing ka mtlb hote hai ki source ip ko change karana. jisase vaha lagata hai ki ye apana hi ip hai. or firewall confuse ho jata hai or us ip ko allow karata h . ","x":375,"y":385,"width":607,"height":85},
		{"id":"d53cf2be62715a48","type":"text","text":"Ip Address Spoofing","x":375,"y":545,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0eba27b33aa9e3ec","type":"text","text":"Mac Address Spoofing","x":375,"y":699,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"33dd4dee33922234","type":"text","text":"Randomize Host Order ek Nmap feature hai jo multiple target hosts ko sequential order me scan karne ke bajay unhe random order me scan karta hai.","x":825,"y":1178,"width":331,"height":115},
		{"id":"5e0190af10f7ff23","type":"text","text":"192.168.1.7\n↓\n\n192.168.1.2\n↓\n\n192.168.1.10\n↓\n\n192.168.1.4\n↓\n\n192.168.1.1","x":1260,"y":1073,"width":135,"height":326},
		{"id":"3a038361afd059c4","type":"text","text":"`nmap --randomize-hosts 192.168.1.0/24`","x":1520,"y":1128,"width":327,"height":50},
		{"id":"2425d836ab19e1a7","type":"text","text":"`nmap --randomize-hosts 10.0.0.1-100`","x":1520,"y":1203,"width":327,"height":60},
		{"id":"8d52a961dcb37550","x":1520,"y":1291,"width":327,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"`nmap --randomize-hosts -iL hosts.txt`"},
		{"id":"50b9ea5b21162d05","x":1949,"y":1263,"width":685,"height":88,"type":"text","text":"Randomize Host Order is an Nmap feature that scans multiple target hosts in a random sequence instead of sequential order. It changes only the order in which hosts are scanned; it does not change the target IP addresses, scan type, or source IP."},
		{"id":"bb9b8eb724413a55","x":1949,"y":1128,"width":685,"height":134,"type":"text","text":"| Randomize Host Order             | Decoy Scan (`-D`)                                       |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Host scan order random karta hai | Multiple source IP addresses use karta hai              |\n| Source IP same rehta hai         | Fake + real source IPs dikh sakte hain                  |\n| Sirf order change hota hai       | Scan traffic multiple sources se aata hua lag sakta hai |\n"},
		{"id":"ccb9fb74b2f14de7","x":3100,"y":1122,"width":540,"height":282,"type":"text","text":"```\nLekin agar tum file se targets read kar rahe ho (-iL) aur unhe random order me scan karna chahte ho, to dono options saath use kar sakte ho:\n```\n\n`nmap -iL targets.txt --randomize-hosts`\n\nYahan:\n\n-iL → Targets file se aayenge.\n--randomize-hosts → Un targets ko random order me scan karega."},
		{"id":"fd7d0131f0571763","x":2666,"y":1138,"width":379,"height":115,"type":"text","text":"-sS → SYN Scan\n-n → DNS lookup mat karo\n-oN result.txt → Output result.txt me save karo\n-iL targets.txt → Targets targets.txt file se lo"},
		{"id":"4fd3d2e56009723e","x":589,"y":1420,"width":567,"height":115,"type":"text","text":"A Proxy Server ek intermediate server hota hai jo client aur destination server ke beech me kaam karta hai. Client ki request pehle proxy server par jati hai, aur proxy us request ko destination server tak forward karta hai. Response bhi pehle proxy ke paas aata hai, phir client ko milta hai."},
		{"id":"f0b8dc1e280c77d9","x":673,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":175,"type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/proxy_server.png"},
		{"id":"6642b2a3ceec5c62","x":395,"y":1940,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Proxy Chaining"},
		{"id":"9edbb88bd8f4fbd2","x":760,"y":1920,"width":398,"height":101,"type":"text","text":"Proxy Chaining ek technique hai jisme ek request ko destination tak pahunchne se pehle ek se zyada proxy servers ke through pass kiya jata ha"},
		{"id":"6e23f2db3201619d","x":1260,"y":1910,"width":400,"height":121,"type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/proxy_chaining.png"},
		{"id":"be41565e7673e24b","x":1200,"y":1478,"width":782,"height":169,"type":"text","text":"| Proxy                                                 | VPN                                                  |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| Specific application ka traffic proxy se ja sakta hai | Device ka almost sara traffic VPN tunnel se jata hai |\n| IP hide kar sakta hai                                 | IP hide karta hai aur traffic encrypt bhi karta hai  |\n| Encryption optional                                   | Encryption normally hoti hai                         |\n| Faster ho sakta hai                                   | Encryption ki wajah se thoda slower ho sakta hai     |\n"},
		{"id":"db0463f981a74403","x":1200,"y":1688,"width":411,"height":169,"type":"text","text":"| Protocol    | Use                               |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------- |\n| HTTP Proxy  | HTTP websites                     |\n| HTTPS Proxy | Secure web traffic                |\n| SOCKS4      | Basic TCP traffic                 |\n| SOCKS5      | TCP + UDP, authentication support |\n"},
		{"id":"224e81240ea7ee0b","x":1640,"y":1688,"width":420,"height":169,"type":"text","text":"Nmap ke kuch features proxies ke saath kaam kar sakte hain (jaise NSE scripts ya version detection ke kuch cases), lekin raw packet scans `(SYN scan -sS, FIN scan -sF, NULL scan -sN, etc.)` generally SOCKS/HTTP proxies ke through nahi chal sakte, kyunki proxies raw IP packets forward nahi karte."}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"5c7869b729890dde","fromNode":"5e8289c9c6cdf6ec","fromSide":"right","toNode":"8c7c238353acbaed","toSide":"left"},
